One facet of the game which I've found useful is to make sure I carry
*everything* downstairs with me.  Sure, it's a lot of work going up and
down the stairs, lugging apparently useless booty, but what the heck?
Eventually you're gonna get a wand of polymorph.  Then you can just sit
back and *make* whatever you need.  You have to make sure you have a lot of
food though.  It takes progressively more time to carry all the treasure.

As the subject line indicates, it doesn't always pay off in your current
lifetime.  Occasionally, you'll hit a bones level that has a ton of stuff
that you left behind in a prior life.  Oh, happy day!

Maybe I just have latent packrat tendencies.

